  "notes": "Mitsubishi currently sells no BEV in Australia (the outgoing eK X EV kei car and i-MiEV were never sold locally, and the Outlander/Eclipse Cross PHEVs are plug-in hybrids, out of scope). The ASX VR-e - Mitsubishi's first BEV confirmed for Australia, built by Foxtron/Foxconn in Taiwan on the 'Foxtron Bria' platform under an OEM arrangement - has been confirmed via Mitsubishi Motors Corporation's own global press release and corroborated by GoAuto/CarExpert for a Q4 2026 Australian launch, with four variant names (LS, Aspire, Exceed, GSR) confirmed. However, as of this September 2026 research date no technical specifications (battery, power, range, charging) or pricing have been released for the Australian market, so all such fields are left null rather than guessed; availability is marked 'announced' since it is a confirmed future AU launch, not yet orderable.",
